== Failure Modes and Mitigations ==

* '''Battery thermal runaway.''' → Cell-level fuse, per-rail current sense, MCU-B watchdog. Worst case: hard-kill lanyard.
* '''Module misidentification.''' → 1-byte identity probe at 3.3 V signalling only before rail power; operator confirmation for unknown IDs.
* '''Operator fatigue / neck strain.''' → Mass cap 850 g Mk1.0, 950 g Mk2.0+; reset reminders every 90 minutes.
* '''Cable snag.''' → All routing internal; single external lanyard with breakaway.
* '''RF emitter stuck-on.''' → MCU-B independently times every emit cycle; hard-cut on watchdog miss.
* '''Cosmetic-only Mk0.0 mistaken for active.''' → Mk0.0 frames carry an internal visible-light-only marker; Mk0.5+ require key-on auth.
* '''Ladder-rung confusion.''' → Each rung is a separate page with its own gates; never assume a Mk2.0 wearer-benefit result implies Mk2.5 stim-payload validity, or vice versa. The legacy 5-step ladder (Mk0/Mk1/Mk1.5/Mk2/Mk3) used in older docs maps non-trivially onto the canonical 7-step — see the §Mk-ladder index below.

